   "lv": "e",
   "q": "What do git diff, git diff --staged and git diff HEAD show?",
   "hint": "Three pairs of areas.",
   "answer": "git diff shows working tree against staging area (unstaged changes). git diff --staged shows staging area against the last commit (what will be committed). git diff HEAD shows working tree against the last commit (everything not committed).",
   "explain": "<p>Running git diff --staged before every commit is a good habit, it catches files you did not mean to include.</p>",
