   "topic": "Branching and merging",
   "lv": "m",
   "q": "Walk me through resolving a merge conflict.",
   "hint": "Markers, edit, add, commit.",
   "answer": "git status lists the unmerged files. Open each one, read the section between the conflict markers, the lines from HEAD and from the other branch, and edit it to the correct final content, removing the markers. Run the tests, git add the file, and git commit to finish the merge. git merge --abort goes back to the state before the merge.",
   "explain": "<p>Setting merge.conflictStyle to zdiff3 also shows the base version, which makes it clear what each side changed.</p>",
   "code": "<<<<<<< HEAD\nreturn round(a / b, 2)\n=======\nreturn a / b if b else None\n>>>>>>> feature",
