   "answer": "Merge joins two lines with a merge commit and keeps history exactly as it happened. Rebase replays your commits on top of another branch, creating new commits with new ids and a straight line. Rebase local work that nobody else has, to tidy it before a pull request. Never rebase commits others have based work on: that is the golden rule.",
   "explain": "<p>A common team rule: rebase your feature branch on main while it is private, merge it into main through a pull request.</p>",
