   "answer": "All three move the current branch to the given commit. --soft stops there, so the undone changes stay staged. --mixed (the default) also resets the staging area, so changes are kept but unstaged. --hard also resets the working tree, so uncommitted changes are discarded.",
   "explain": "<p>Only --hard can lose work you never committed. Commits that the branch no longer points to can still be found with git reflog for a while.</p>",
