   "answer": "With stages, every job of a stage waits for the whole previous stage, so the slowest job of each stage sets the pace. With needs, a job waits only for the jobs it names, so the pipeline time becomes the longest path through the job graph. Example: build jobs of 2 and 9 minutes and a 3 minute test that needs only the 2 minute job take 12 minutes with stages and 9 with needs.",
